 "_comment": "Issue #163: THE rank-scaled bounty canonical. A SILVER-rank player (swordsman 13, power 13.0) at the guild board. Proves, in order: (1) player_rank derives to 'silver' from effective_power; (2) accepting bounty_gossip_tea resolves+LOCKS its SILVER tier (accepted_bounty_tier 'silver'), and the journal's Postings detail shows the SILVER copy verbatim + the SILVER 8-gold payout (the 'board shows silver copy' proof -- exact-string, off the same ui_journal_shown surface journal_history pins bronze copy on); (3) completion via the delta-since-accept contract over the SILVER condition (heard_gossip 5, vs bronze 3) -- talk pools across a real sleep, which also proves the tier stays LOCKED at silver through the sleep; (4) turn-in pays the SILVER 8 gold (gold_changed delta 8, not the bronze 2). CAN-FAIL (documented, proven at authoring): change the silver tier's gold to 6 in bounties.json -> the turn-in gold_changed delta assert (8) fails red; revert. Fixture rng_state governs; seed 9 for convention (no combat).",
